The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches why motorcycles are misjudged and how to follow and pass them, the truck no-zones and wide turns, the slow moving vehicle emblem and passing farm equipment, how to respond to aggressive drivers, the duties around ridden and driven animals, and the moose and deer hazard. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
